PATCH 585: the player-loss flash -- a5c4's three immediates (red 64, green 32, blue 32 frames) and the
063c/0655 waits.

board:0002.  When the player's vehicle is destroyed, a93e's a5c4 (`push di ; push [0x452] ; mov ax,0x40 ;
mov si,0x20 ; mov di,0x20 ; lcall [0x5c4] ; pop [0x452] ; pop di ; retf`) runs MGAVIDEO 063c: 0647 sets
the DAC run (bx = 0, cx = 0xff, dx = 0xffff) and 0660 arms the per-channel fade 0732 -- each channel's
accumulator counts up at 0x10000/frames per retrace, the intensity table is i * (0x10000 - acc) >> 16,
so a channel dims to black over its frame count and stays there once the accumulator wraps (rate and
accumulator both 0); when all three are 0 the stepper unregisters.  063c then spins on 09c6 (`call 9c6 ;
jb`) until it has.  The oracle's register trace (scratch/oracle/regtrace_0660) shows AX = 0x40, SI = DI =
0x20 at 0660 on every player loss.

Ghidra dropped the three immediates at a5c4's indirect call, so the port's 0660 took whatever lay on the
stack -- in AZER1 red 16992, green 32, blue 51752: green black in 32 frames, blue in one, red dimming for
21845 frames -- and 063c's wait was folded to one pass, so the cockpit switch ran under the tint instead
of after the fade.  Every frame after the switch was red (FIST_DUMPTICK 1860..4000).  With the
immediates and the wait, the fade runs to black in 64 retraces and the switch follows it, as the
original's.  0655 (`call 660 ; call 9c6 ; jb`) carried the same folded wait.

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
